WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.050
Who decides the next step?

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.324
That one question separates a workflow from a loop.

00:00:05.424 --> 00:00:09.918
In a workflow, we chose it. In a loop, the model does.

00:00:11.118 --> 00:00:16.572
A loop runs think, act, observe, decide, on repeat.

00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:20.358
In a workflow, the steps are written in advance,

00:00:20.408 --> 00:00:26.315
and the same input takes the same path. In a loop, the model chooses at run time,

00:00:26.365 --> 00:00:27.784
so two runs can differ.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:34.186
Every loop that survives production has four parts. A goal with a testable done.

00:00:34.236 --> 00:00:40.100
A checker outside the model. A stop rule. And a budget in turns and dollars.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.424
Why outside? Because self-review is not a checker.

00:00:44.974 --> 00:00:51.172
In practice, filter first. Loop briefly. Then fall back to a fixed path.

00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:56.702
Atlan's filter stopped roughly eighty-six percent of alerts before a single token was spent.

00:00:57.252 --> 00:01:03.042
That's module two, loop. Start with page one: Loops versus workflows.
